{title: Nothing Deserving Death}
{subtitle: Acts 25:13; 25:23; 26:1–30; 26:30–32}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Some days later in Caesarea town
The King and his [Cm7]sister arrived now
To pay their re[Ab]spects to the new governor
With [Bb]great pomp they entered the hall of pow[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Paul was brought in at the order of Festus
[Cm7]To speak his defense before the men
The [Ab]King gave him permission to speak
[Bb]And Paul stretched out his hand in the end
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This man has [Eb]done nothing deserving death
Or imprisonment [Cm7]for the charges laid
He spoke of [Ab]light and of the risen Lord
And they agreed [Bb]that no guilt was weighed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I saw a [Eb]light brighter than the sun
Blazing [Cm7]around me on the road to Damascus
The Lord said [Ab]I am Jesus whom you perse[Bb]cute
Arise and stand on your feet, it was said
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
I [Eb]was not disobedient to the vision
I [Cm7]preached to Damascus and Jerusalem
To [Ab]Israel and the Gentiles alike
That [Bb]they should repent and turn to Him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This man has [Eb]done nothing deserving death
Or imprisonment [Cm7]for the charges laid
He spoke of [Ab]light and of the risen Lord
And they a[Bb]greed that no guilt was [Abmaj7]weighed
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Abmaj7] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Abmaj7] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The [Ab]King rose up with the governor
And Ber[Bb]nice and those who were seated
As they [Ab]withdrew they spoke to one another
[Bb]With words of truth that they believed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He [Ab]could have been set free if he had not ap[Bb]pealed
To Caesar's court in the [Eb]end
{end_of_verse}

